                    {
                        "recommendationid": "228019420",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198132276974",
                            "num_reviews": 165,
                            "playtime_forever": 507,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 507,
                            "last_played": 1652750705
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "When I played this initially way back in the day, I found the game's mechanics fell apart as soon as you got more then one ship. For some bizarre reason, the game required you to switch your screen to that particular ship in order to move it which made combat unnecessarily frustrating. The last time I came back to this game, there was an update that made the UI worse.\n\nI have no real desire to return to it. The only reason I got it was because on release, it was one of the few space sims to actually allow you to land your ship on planets and space stations and have your crew disembark and do things, and I wanted a good point to jump into the genre. While still not entirely prevalent nowadays, there are more and better options for that now. I don't think there's a reason to play this in today's market.",
